  "preconditions": [
    "Explicit owned descriptor or None, available input bytes or None, and independently supplied logical-path roles or None. No host discovery or inferred file roles.",
    "12.m.W: Owned TargetModel plus explicit evaluation and configuration, with optional independent native scope bindings. Only supplied Evidence is observed; input bytes and roles are assessed separately."
  ],
  "steps": [
    "Retain W manifest/hash and isolated runtime checks. Check exact role/byte binding, reject Evidence/output/descriptor/selection inputs without filtering, preserve missing binding observations as incomplete/SRV176, verify ownership and isolated Core/PYZ.",
    "12.m.W: Build independent obligations first, then retain the union of declared expected runs and all matching supplied observations; require exact product/key/configuration binding and preserve each Evidence result, including simultaneous failure after a later success. Check multiple slots and subjects, missing declarations, native run conflicts, ownership and isolated Core/PYZ contracts."
  ],
  "oracle": {
    "kind": "behavior",
    "requirement_contract": "Ein Requirement DARF das berechnete `verification_result=passed` nur nach vollständiger Bewertungs- und Nachweisauswahl sowie erfolgreicher Aggregation nach Kapitel 10.5 besitzen.",
    "scope": "12.k.W/R: Actual bytes bind product and descriptor hashes. Explicit checker/importer role inventory excludes Evidence, check outputs, evaluation and selection metadata from inputs; unlisted declared inputs cannot disappear. Missing evaluation or unavailable binding is incomplete/SRV176; forbidden manifest roles are SRV175/code 3. Ready means input binding only, never passed or external execution/approval. Roles are declared, not authenticated. 12.m.W selects all supplied same-product observed and expected run candidates per independent key, preserving every raw result and original Evidence binding. Bound configuration must match; cross-configuration independence requires an explicit current contract. Selection is not freshness, replacement, final aggregation or a passed verification result."
  },
